<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abdurrahman Melek</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1896">1896</a>–<a href="/years/1978">1978</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abdurrahman Melek was prime minister of the Hatay State, the short-lived republic formed in 1938 from the Sanjak of Alexandretta under French and Turkish supervision. He governed alongside the head of state <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tayfur-sokmen">Tayfur Sökmen</a> while the state adopted Turkish laws, currency and symbols, until its annexation by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkey">Turkey</a> in 1939.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/abdurrahman-melek.jpg" alt="Abdurrahman Melek" width="180" height="236" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Abdur_rahman_Melek.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
